  "verbalization": "Calabaxanthone is linked to VMRC-MELG through a series of molecular interactions, primarily through its targeting of 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is a known target of Calabaxanthone, and it, in turn, is targeted by a complex steroid-like molecule, which is also a target of VMRC-MELG. This suggests that Calabaxanthone may act through a pathway involving the proteasome, potentially modulating the activity of this subunit, which is a key component in the regulation of protein degradation. The evidence points to a possible role of Calabaxanthone in influencing the proteasome system, which could have downstream effects on cellular processes mediated by VMRC-MELG. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism by which Calabaxanthone may interact with VMRC-MELG, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
